Ladybird’s find-in-page searches the documents of a page in tree order,
the top-level document first. Chromium’s FindRequestManager searches
every frame of a page, walking the frame tree with TraverseNext(), and
Firefox’s nsWebBrowserFind searches subframes with SearchInFrame() (from
reading the sources; the report says both find the iframe’s text). In
all three engines, window.find() searches only its own window, as it
does in Ladybird (run in Chrome 158, Firefox 151, and WebKit 26.5).
